IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc1-common`
IMPORT `uc1-part3-awards`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 4, the general provisions: regulation 36 (the table of the
-- amounts of the elements) and regulation 37 (run-on after a death).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE: the figures of the table, one rule per row, and the run-on after a death. The other modules of Part 4 call
-- these rules (regulation 24 for the child element, 27 for the LCWRA element, 29 for the carer element, 34 for the childcare
-- costs element); regulation 36 is read-only data for them.
-- Money is a NUMBER of pounds; 338.58 is three hundred and thirty-eight pounds and 58 pence.
-- Rows of the table that the text shows as repealed (the first-child rate of 351.88 and the first row of the LCWRA element) are
-- not encoded as amounts: see fork F-36-REPEALED in NOTES.md.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 36(1) and (3): the standard allowance. Age is a NUMBER of complete years at the first day of the assessment
-- period (the text gives no date for "aged under 25": fork F-36-AGE, assumed and not ruled). A member of a couple who claims as a
-- single person gets the single claimant's amount (paragraph (3)). The other member's age is read only for joint claimants.
-- src:715 | (3) In the case of an award where the claimant is a member of a couple, but claims as a single person, the amounts are those shown in the table for a single claimant.
-- src:717 | | Standard allowance |
-- src:718 | | | single claimant aged under 25 | £338.58 |
-- src:719 | | | single claimant aged 25 or over | £424.90 |
-- src:720 | | | joint claimants both aged under 25 | £528.34 |
-- src:721 | | | joint claimants where either is aged 25 or over | £666.97 |
@ref reg 36(1) and (3), table: standard allowance (src:715-721)
GIVEN `claim basis` IS A `Claim basis`
      `age of the claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `age of the other member of the couple` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 36(1) — the standard allowance` `claim basis` `age of the claimant` `age of the other member of the couple` MEANS
    CONSIDER `claim basis`
    WHEN `a single claimant` THEN
        IF `age of the claimant` LESS THAN 25 THEN 338.58 ELSE 424.90
    WHEN `a single claimant who is a member of a couple` THEN
        IF `age of the claimant` LESS THAN 25 THEN 338.58 ELSE 424.90
    WHEN `joint claimants` THEN
        IF (`age of the claimant` LESS THAN 25) AND (`age of the other member of the couple` LESS THAN 25)
        THEN 528.34
        ELSE 666.97

-- The child element: one amount for each child or qualifying young person. The table shows the first-child row as repealed and
-- the second-and-subsequent row as "each child or qualifying young person" at 303.94; the encoding takes the second to apply to
-- every child (fork F-36-REPEALED).
-- src:722 | | Child element— |
-- src:723 | | | {repealed: first child or qualifying young person} | {repealed: £351.88} |
-- src:724 | | | {repealed: second and each subsequent}each child or qualifying young person | £303.94 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: child element (src:722-724)
`reg 36(1) — the amount of the child element for each child or qualifying young person` MEANS 303.94

-- The additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person (regulation 24(2) says which rate applies).
-- src:725 | | Additional amount for disabled child or qualifying young person— |
-- src:726 | | | lower rate | £164.79 |
-- src:727 | | | higher rate | £514.71 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person (src:725-727)
DECLARE `Rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` IS ONE OF
    `the lower rate`
    `the higher rate`
    `no additional amount`

-- src:725 | | Additional amount for disabled child or qualifying young person— |
-- src:726 | | | lower rate | £164.79 |
-- src:727 | | | higher rate | £514.71 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person (src:725-727)
GIVEN rate IS A `Rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 36(1) — the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` rate MEANS
    CONSIDER rate
    WHEN `the lower rate` THEN 164.79
    WHEN `the higher rate` THEN 514.71
    WHEN `no additional amount` THEN 0

-- The LCWRA element: 429.80 for a pre-2026 claimant, a severe conditions criteria claimant or a claimant who is terminally ill;
-- 217.26 for any other claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity. The first row of the element is
-- dots in this text and is not encoded (fork F-36-REPEALED).
-- src:728 | | LCWRA element— |
-- src:730 | | | claimant with limited capability for work and work-related activity, other than a pre-2026 claimant, a severe conditions criteria claimant or a claimant who is terminally ill | £217.26 |
-- src:731 | | | pre-2026 claimant, severe conditions criteria claimant or claimant who is terminally ill | £429.80 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: LCWRA element (src:728-731)
GIVEN `the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Part 5 (piece uc4)
      `the claimant is terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN  -- keel: regulation 2 defines this; the seat passes in the result of `reg 2 — terminally ill`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 36(1) — the amount of the LCWRA element` `the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant` `the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant` `the claimant is terminally ill` MEANS
    IF (`the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant`) OR (`the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant`) OR (`the claimant is terminally ill`)
    THEN 429.80
    ELSE 217.26

-- src:732 | | Carer element | £209.34 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: carer element (src:732)
`reg 36(1) — the amount of the carer element` MEANS 209.34

-- The maximum amount of the childcare costs element: 1,071.09 for one child, 1,836.16 for two or more. For no child there is no
-- row, and the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:733 | | Childcare costs element— | |
-- src:734 | | | maximum amount for one child | £1,071.09 |
-- src:735 | | | maximum amount for two or more children | £1,836.16 |
@ref reg 36(1), table: childcare costs element (src:733-735)
GIVEN `number of children in respect of whom childcare charges are paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 36(1) — the maximum amount of the childcare costs element` `number of children in respect of whom childcare charges are paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `number of children in respect of whom childcare charges are paid` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 1071.09
        IF `number of children in respect of whom childcare charges are paid` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST 1836.16
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 37: run-on after a death.
-- Where one member of a couple in a joint award, a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible, a severely
-- disabled person for whom a claimant had regular and substantial caring responsibilities, or a non-dependant within the meaning of
-- paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4 has died, the maximum amount of the award continues to be calculated as if the person had not died
-- for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two.
-- src:737 | In calculating the maximum amount of an award where any of the following persons has died—
-- src:738 | (a) in the case of a joint award, one member of the couple;
-- src:739 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible; ...
-- src:740 | (c) in the case of a claimant who had regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person, that person; or
-- src:741 | (d) a person who was a non-dependant within the meaning of paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4,
-- src:742 | the award is to continue to be calculated as if the person had not died for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two assessment periods.
@ref reg 37 (src:737-742)
DECLARE `Person whose death does not at once change the maximum amount of an award` IS ONE OF
    `one member of the couple, in the case of a joint award`
    `a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible`
    `a severely disabled person for whom a claimant had regular and substantial caring responsibilities`
    `a non-dependant within the meaning of paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4`
    `another person`

-- src:737 | In calculating the maximum amount of an award where any of the following persons has died—
-- src:738 | (a) in the case of a joint award, one member of the couple;
-- src:739 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible; ...
-- src:740 | (c) in the case of a claimant who had regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person, that person; or
-- src:741 | (d) a person who was a non-dependant within the meaning of paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4,
-- src:742 | the award is to continue to be calculated as if the person had not died for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two assessment periods.
@ref reg 37 (src:737-742)
GIVEN `person who has died` IS A `Person whose death does not at once change the maximum amount of an award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37 — the death is of a person that the regulation names` `person who has died` MEANS
    NOT (`person who has died` EQUALS `another person`)

-- The award is calculated as if the person had not died for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two.
-- The periods are those of regulation 21, counted from the first date of entitlement. If no assessment period of the award contains
-- the day of the death (the death is before the award began) the regulation has nothing to run on from, and the answer is FALSE.
-- src:742 | the award is to continue to be calculated as if the person had not died for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two assessment periods.
@ref reg 37 (src:742)
GIVEN `first date of entitlement` IS A DATE
      `day of the death` IS A DATE
      `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37 — the assessment period is one for which the person is treated as not having died` `first date of entitlement` `day of the death` `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 21(1) — the position of the assessment period containing a day` `first date of entitlement` `day of the death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `position of the period of the death` THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 21(1) — the position of the assessment period containing a day` `first date of entitlement` `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST `position of the period asked about` THEN
            (`position of the period asked about` AT LEAST `position of the period of the death`)
            AND (`position of the period asked about` AT MOST (`position of the period of the death` PLUS 2))

-- Both questions together.
-- src:737 | In calculating the maximum amount of an award where any of the following persons has died—
-- src:738 | (a) in the case of a joint award, one member of the couple;
-- src:739 | (b) a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant was responsible; ...
-- src:740 | (c) in the case of a claimant who had regular and substantial caring responsibilities for a severely disabled person, that person; or
-- src:741 | (d) a person who was a non-dependant within the meaning of paragraph 9(2) of Schedule 4,
-- src:742 | the award is to continue to be calculated as if the person had not died for the assessment period in which the death occurs and the following two assessment periods.
@ref reg 37 (src:737-742)
GIVEN `person who has died` IS A `Person whose death does not at once change the maximum amount of an award`
      `first date of entitlement` IS A DATE
      `day of the death` IS A DATE
      `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37 — the maximum amount is calculated as if the person had not died` `person who has died` `first date of entitlement` `day of the death` `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated` MEANS
    (`reg 37 — the death is of a person that the regulation names` `person who has died`)
    AND (`reg 37 — the assessment period is one for which the person is treated as not having died` `first date of entitlement` `day of the death` `a day in the assessment period for which the maximum amount is calculated`)
